    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1946-10-11">October 11, 1946</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Mr.
                        Kauder</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>Thank you for <rs ref="L11009" type="letter">your letter of September 29th</rs>
                    and <rs type="work" ref="#tillich__PIFTF5XH">your reprint</rs>. I liked it very
                    much and learned a good deal from it. I have not answered your letter because I
                    was not able to give you a weekend in which I was certain to be in <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs>. Besides that I do
                    not think that a conversation with me would be worthwhile a trip from <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__754" type="place">Detroit</rs> to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs>. Your reprint and
                    your letter show me that I can recommend you as much as <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1965" type="person">Ulich</rs> and <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__710" type="person">Prof. Grant</rs> did. But I want
                    to give you a concrete advise. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1844" type="person"
                        >Mrs. Else Staudinger</rs> has a Committee for Refugee Scholars. She has
                    written to all universities and colleges and has received a large number of
                    requests. I suggest that you send her your material and refer to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1965" type="person">Prof. Ulich</rs>, <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__710" type="person">Prof. Grant</rs> and myself in
                    your letter to her. The address is: AMERICAN COMMITTEE FOR REFUGEE SCHOLARS, 66
                    Fifth Avenue <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York
                    City</rs>.</p>
                <closer><salute>I am looking forward to <rs type="work" ref="#tillich__C5UTEQ4H"
                            >your next reprint</rs>. With all my good wishes,<lb/>Yours
                        sincerely,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person"
                            >Prof. Paul Tillich</rs></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
